  "claim": "The Soul of Buddha is a 1918 American silent romance film shot in a borough that is the western terminus of the George Washington Bridge.",
  "evidencia": "Page: The Soul of Buddha. Sentence: The Soul of Buddha is a 1918 American silent romance film directed by J. Gordon Edwards and starring Theda Bara, who also wrote the film's story.\nPage: The Soul of Buddha. Sentence: The film was produced by Fox Film Corporation and shot at the Fox Studio in Fort Lee, New Jersey.\nPage: Fort Lee, New Jersey. Sentence: Fort Lee is a borough at the eastern border of Bergen County, New Jersey, United States, in the New York City Metropolitan Area, situated atop the Hudson Palisades.\nPage: Fort Lee, New Jersey. Sentence: The borough is the western terminus of the George Washington Bridge and is located across the Hudson River from the Manhattan borough of New York City.",
  "evidence_text": "Page: The Soul of Buddha. Sentence: The Soul of Buddha is a 1918 American silent romance film directed by J. Gordon Edwards and starring Theda Bara, who also wrote the film's story.\nPage: The Soul of Buddha. Sentence: The film was produced by Fox Film Corporation and shot at the Fox Studio in Fort Lee, New Jersey.\nPage: Fort Lee, New Jersey. Sentence: Fort Lee is a borough at the eastern border of Bergen County, New Jersey, United States, in the New York City Metropolitan Area, situated atop the Hudson Palisades.\nPage: Fort Lee, New Jersey. Sentence: The borough is the western terminus of the George Washington Bridge and is located across the Hudson River from the Manhattan borough of New York City.",
