        "original_id": "d6fdf620-fd26-59e2-8ba7-587c19283975",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: The Soul of Buddha\n- People: J. Gordon Edwards, Theda Bara\n- Companies: Fox Film Corporation\n- Places: Fort Lee, New Jersey; Bergen County; Hudson Palisades; Hudson River; Manhattan; New York City Metropolitan Area; George Washington Bridge\n\nFacts:\n- The Soul of Buddha is a 1918 American silent romance film.\n- J. Gordon Edwards directed The Soul of Buddha.\n- Theda Bara starred in The Soul of Buddha and wrote the film's story.\n- Fox Film Corporation produced The Soul of Buddha.\n- The Soul of Buddha was shot at the Fox Studio in Fort Lee, New Jersey.\n- Fort Lee is a borough on the eastern border of Bergen County, New Jersey, in the United States.\n- Fort Lee is in the New York City Metropolitan Area and sits atop the Hudson Palisades.\n- Fort Lee is the western terminus of the George Washington Bridge.\n- Fort Lee is across the Hudson River from Manhattan in New York City.",
